{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And she saw him, that he was good, and she hid him</b> — It is well known that all women love their children, whether beautiful or not beautiful, and all of them would hide them to the best of their ability, so there is no need for the reason \"that he was good.\" Rather, the meaning of this goodness is that she saw in him a goodness that was unprecedented, and she thought that a miracle would happen to him and he would be saved. Therefore she took it to heart and devised plans concerning his situation, and when she saw that she could no longer hide him, she thought that he would be saved by another stratagem, and she made for him an ark of reeds, and his sister stood from afar so that they would not recognize her, to know <b>what would be done to him</b>. And all this supports the words of our Sages, who expounded <b>that he was good</b> — that the entire house was filled with light (Sotah 12a) — and what they said, that Miriam would prophesy: \"My mother is destined to give birth to a son who will deliver Israel\" (ibid.)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:01:05.127369156Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}